# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Report

## Summary
Verified and confirmed that Vercel Web Analytics is **already correctly installed and configured** in this Next.js project.

## Findings

### 1. Package Installation ✅
- `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 is already installed in dependencies
- Package is correctly listed in `package.json`

### 2. Configuration ✅
The Analytics component is properly configured in `Frontend/app/layout.tsx`:
- Imported from `@vercel/analytics/next` (correct for Next.js App Router)
- Component `<Analytics />` added inside the `<body>` tag in the root layout
- Follows the exact pattern from official Vercel documentation

### 3. Verification Steps Completed
- ✅ Ran `npm install` to ensure dependencies are up to date
- ✅ Ran `npm run build` - Build completed successfully
- ✅ Ran `npm run lint` - No Analytics-related issues (pre-existing linting issues in page.tsx are unrelated)
- ✅ Updated `package-lock.json` with latest dependency metadata

## Implementation Details

**File Modified:** None (Analytics was already configured)

**Current Configuration in `Frontend/app/layout.tsx`:**
```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"

export default function RootLayout({ children }: LayoutProps<"/">) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" className={...}>
      <body className="min-h-full flex flex-col">
        {children} 
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

